{
  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, singleprofile, PCA n2000 → acc 0.485), the dominant uncertainty is whether the image modality contributes any predictive signal beyond RNA. config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, PCA n2000, resnet50, concat) is the cleanest single-axis extension of config_001: it keeps the RNA encoder and profile setting identical and adds only the image modality with the simplest possible fusion (concat) and a standard backbone (resnet50). If it outperforms 0.485, we confirm image adds value and should next probe fusion strategy and image encoder; if it does not, we learn that basic multimodal fusion is insufficient and should focus on RNA encoder upgrades or more sophisticated fusion. This experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the study's central design question (modality contribution) while changing the fewest variables relative to the existing baseline, making it the most information-dense use of the next budget slot."
}

